<!-- Single-colour silhouette for Android 13+ themed icons (Settings > Wallpaper & style >
     Themed icons). The system throws the colours away and tints the silhouette, so everything
     that tells one building from another has to live in the shape.

     That is why the silhouette is NOT one solid block: gaps are left between buildings that
     touch, and the windows are holes (evenOdd). Without colour they are the only thing that
     makes the heights and the pieces read instead of a single mass. Filling them in "to
     simplify" deletes the drawing: do not.

     The gaps measured on this pathData, edge to edge: 1.59 dp between bar and tree, 1.60
     between spired tower and bar, 2.40 between small house and domed tower, 2.90 for the other
     two pairs. The tightest is 1.59 dp. A launcher shows the middle 72 dp of this canvas, so 1
     dp is size/72 pixels: that gap is 4.2 px on a 192 px icon but only 1.06 px at 48 px. It is
     the first thing to close if anyone thickens the silhouette.

     Containment: 27.95 dp from the centre against a safe radius of 33 dp, so 5.05 dp of margin. -->
